landing-review: play revision (f9be7b67..1744f963, one play revision a game) -- one high-effort read-only review of f9be7b67. The stub, every joiner path (21 bytes, 301, tail at revision 0/1/2, no row), the read through the engine's own edi, the released hosts v0.4..v0.6.1 and the addresses in the notes verified against the disassembly and the tags. MEDIUM: a player made without the revision (the test lever, a failed key, network sites that do not go in) could reach a stock or older host while the stream sent four messages a tick -- fixed: several messages only while the process holds the revision (tagpu_rec_mp_revision_held), a failed key sends the 21 bytes at the revision. LOW, fixed: the create comment, five overclaims in the notes on which release refuses by size and which by the WORD, modmp's olderhost could not tell a refusal from a crash, mp_init did not match the bytes the stub resumes into (0x45435B, 14 bytes). NOTE, taken: the read's argument restated; codeduel's two DLLs share a revision. NOTE, left: a no-fingerprint player of this build is still named an older build. The fixes were run (modmp older/olderhost/stock with v0.6.1 and v0.5; mp_agree --marches 10 plain and --host-as-stock) and not reviewed again. Stated gap: a launch whose network sites do not go in plays as stock with the other fail-closed simulation fixes in.
